Why this change (Ralph loop log):

Context discovered: IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md and specs/ both described a
completed Space Invaders game (100% done), but the working tree held large
uncommitted work pivoting the app to a "Codebase Execution-Flow Explorer".
Session-store history (prior cloud sessions) confirmed the user explicitly
asked to "reimplement this app and make it completely focus on the code
repository visualization, quizzing the student to identify the flow of
execution in a given github repo that they provide." So the docs were stale,
not the code.

Verification performed before committing:
- pytest 10 passed, vitest 2 passed, Playwright 3 passed.
- mypy/flake8/tsc/eslint clean; vite production build clean.
- Live end-to-end check of analyze_repository against EXTERNAL repos
  (pallets/click, psf/requests) returned 4 import-chain flows each. This
  confirms the prior open bug ("only works with ralph-wiggum repo") is fixed:
  the generic Python/JS-TS import-chain detection now runs as a fallback
  alongside the Flask+Islands request-flow detection, so arbitrary repos work.

Design rationale captured for future loops:
- Answer keys live server-side in an in-memory TTL snapshot store; the learner
  payload sorts steps by path so the correct execution order is never leaked
  to the browser (anti-cheat). No DB persistence by design (privacy, snapshots
  are short-lived).
- Fixture repos under tests/fixtures/repositories exist so pytest/E2E run
  deterministically offline; enabled via LEARNING_ALLOW_FIXTURE_REPOS (off in
  dev/prod, on in TestingConfig and the Playwright webServer env).

Tooling note: pre-commit mypy/flake8 were typechecking the fixture sample
repos (intentionally simple/buggy sample code) and failing. Excluded
tests/fixtures from those hooks; pytest already skips them via norecursedirs.

Spec hygiene: removed specs/space-invaders-classic-gameplay.md and added
specs/codebase-execution-flow-explorer.md (single source of truth).
